From 794c029d592b0e47e5698da855c995dad4bbb586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Koenig <tkoenig@gcc.gnu.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:24:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] LEADZ, POPCNT, POPPAR and TRAILZ for unsigned numbers.

Playing around with UNSIGNED, I noted that LEADZ and TRAILZ were rejected
for UNSIGNED, which makes no sense.  POPCNT and POPPAR worked, but this
was not documented.  All that was needed for the LEADZ and TRAILZ to work
was to adjust the check routine.

gcc/fortran/ChangeLog:

	PR fortran/128124
	* gfortran.texi: Note that LEADZ, POPCNT, POPPAR and TRAILZ take
	unsigned arguments.
	* intrinsic.cc (add_functions): LEADZ and TRAILZ also take unsigned
	arguments.
	* intrinsic.texi: Document unsigned arguments for LEADZ, POPCNT, POPPAR
	and TRAILZ.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	PR fortran/128124
	* gfortran.dg/unsigned_45.f90: New test.

(cherry picked from commit bd6079f1a465fad5c9916bcad71c583a69fbd281)
